@@ -16,7 +16,34 @@ Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History
 - Storage key: `todos-vanillajs` per spec convention (`todos-[framework]`).
 - Tier: happy-dom (default). The spec requires DOM rendering; happy-dom is the cheapest tier that observes it.
 - Scantling for localStorage shape at `scantlings/todo-storage.json`.
+- Scantling for DOM element identity at `scantlings/dom-identity.json`.
+
+## Defects found
+
+**Real-browser DOM-identity defects.** Acceptance suite (Cypress, real browser) reports 10 failures. All trace to one root cause: `render()` in `js/app.js` does `todoList.innerHTML = ''` on every state change, destroying and recreating all `<li>` elements.
+
+1. **Toggle-all / toggle-item (failures 1-4):** `render()` rebuilds the todo list, invalidating element references the browser held — Cypress reports "element detached from DOM".
+2. **Editing visibility (failures 5-10):** The `dblclick` handler calls `render()` then does `li.querySelector('.edit')` on the old, detached `<li>`. The detached element's `.edit` input has `display: none` (no `.editing` class on the detached subtree), so Cypress cannot interact with it. The `focus()` call on a `display:none` element does nothing in a real browser.
+
+**In-harness suite passes** because steps bypass the real event handling (editing is triggered via localStorage writes, not actual `dblclick`). This is expected for a browser-only defect.
+
+## Spec changes this cycle
+
+- Added 5 @browser scenarios to `features/todo-management.feature` (DOM element identity for toggle, toggle-all, editing visibility, edit-mode focus).
+- Added 1 @conformance scenario to `features/todo-management.feature` referencing `scantlings/dom-identity.json` — can pass in happy-dom via source-level pattern check.
+- Created `scantlings/dom-identity.json` defining forbidden patterns (innerHTML replacement) and required patterns (classList.toggle, in-document focus).
+- Created `watchbill.json` with all scenario references grouped by watch.
+
+## Fix required
+
+The fix is production-code only (Captain does not implement):
+- **Replace `todoList.innerHTML = ''` pattern** with in-place mutation: toggle `className` / `classList` on existing `<li>` elements instead of destroying and recreating them.
+- **After `render()` in the dblclick handler**, query the NEW `<li>` for the `.edit` input and focus it, not the old detached reference.
+- Alternative: skip `render()` entirely for completion-toggling (just toggle the class and checkbox in place) and for editing (just toggle the `.editing` class and show/hide the edit input).
 
 ## Next
 
-Dispatch QM with `watchbill.json` targets when production code exists.
